    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": ">24 h of inpatient observation is recommended; IV regimens as for PID (eg, ceftriaxone 1 g IV q24h + doxycycline + metronidazole)"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Complete 14 days with oral doxycycline plus clindamycin 450 mg QID or metronidazole 500 mg BID, for better anaerobic coverage"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Ampicillin-sulbactam + doxycycline is effective against C. trachomatis, N. gonorrhoeae and anaerobes in TOA"
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
